Spec: Todo Form Component

Purpose:
  Provide the new-todo input and notify the parent when a valid title is submitted.

Structure:
  ./todo-form.js: Todo form component implementation.

Owns:
  ./todo-form.js

Must:
  Render a text input and a submit mechanism (button or Enter key).
  Clear the input after a successful submit.
  Invoke the @onAdd callback with the trimmed title.
  Reject submission if the trimmed title is empty.

Must not:
  Call @TodoService directly.
  Contain business logic beyond input trimming and empty-check.

Exposes:
  @TodoForm

Accepts:
  @onAdd callback that receives the trimmed title.

Scenario: valid submission
  Given the input contains a non-empty title
  When the user submits
  Then @onAdd is called with the trimmed title
  And the input is cleared

Scenario: empty submission
  Given the input is empty or whitespace
  When the user submits
  Then @onAdd is not called
  And the input remains focused

Done when:
  Valid submissions call @onAdd with the trimmed title.
  Input clears after valid submission.
  Empty submissions keep focus without calling @onAdd.
